    "created_at": "2018-06-20T15:32:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-06-20T15:32:13Z",
    "body": "Given the choice between default == false and default == true, I’m biased towards default == false, which would imply the property should be `preferNoNavigationBar`.\r\n\r\nBut this may be a false choice; another option would be to target the use case and not the behavior. So, given the discussion in #123, this could be `prefersMinimalUI: true` or `presentationStyle: “video”` or something along those lines. Samsung could interpret that as “hide the nav bar”, without actually writing “navigation bar” into the spec. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "reactions": {
