    "created_at": "2018-08-24T04:43:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-24T04:43:20Z",
    "body": "On the one hand, navigation bar doesn't sound like a general concept should be put into the spec. Specifically, Android is probably the only platform has such concept. None of desktop platforms, nor iOS has it. Meanwhile, desktop browsers have a \"location bar\" include some navigation functionality, which makes it feel confusing in terminology.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, for a more general concept like \"minimalUI\", I'm concerned about how implementations would interpret that. What does \"minimal\" means? Should desktop browsers show something like... system taskbar or window controls? It feels quite vague.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
